Then identify its homologous series, and show that

141
00:06:06,134 --> 00:06:08,453
propyne fits its general formula.

142
00:06:08,774 --> 00:06:09,973
Pause here to answer.

143
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:22,640
The C H three carbon has four single

144
00:06:22,720 --> 00:06:26,240
bonds: tetrahedral, about one hundred and nine point

145
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:27,200
five degrees.

146
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:29,680
The two carbons in the triple bond each

147
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:33,440
have two directions: linear, one hundred and eighty.

148
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:36,560
Propyne is an alkyne, C n H two

149
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:38,160
n minus two.

150
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:40,320
With n equal to three, that's C three

151
00:06:40,560 --> 00:06:42,240
H four, which matches.

152
00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:45,280
Calling all three carbons linear misses the C

153
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:46,080
H three.

154
00:06:47,300 --> 00:06:47,940
Last one.

155
00:06:48,220 --> 00:06:52,740
Hexane and two, three-dimethylbutane both have the molecular

156
00:06:52,820 --> 00:06:55,620
formula C six H fourteen.

157
00:06:55,940 --> 00:06:58,620
Explain which has the higher boiling point.

158
00:06:58,900 --> 00:07:02,900
Refer to the intramolecular and intermolecular bonding present.

159
00:07:03,220 --> 00:07:04,500
Pause here to answer.

160
00:07:14,900 --> 00:07:18,900
Inside each molecule, covalent bonds hold the atoms,

161
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:20,660
and boiling doesn't break them.

162
00:07:21,220 --> 00:07:24,100
Both have the same electrons, and only dispersion

163
00:07:24,180 --> 00:07:26,060
forces between molecules.

164
00:07:26,340 --> 00:07:29,300
Hexane's straight chain lies alongside its neighbours with

165
00:07:29,380 --> 00:07:32,980
more contact, so its dispersion forces are stronger,

166
00:07:33,020 --> 00:07:34,660
and it has the higher boiling point.

167
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:37,940
Saying the branched one has weaker covalent bonds

168
00:07:38,020 --> 00:07:41,380
is wrong: boiling separates molecules.

169
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:44,480
So the bond type sets the shape at

170
00:07:44,520 --> 00:07:47,080
each carbon, and size and shape set the

171
00:07:47,160 --> 00:07:48,920
forces between molecules.

